# Code style

Full guide: [docs/CODE_STYLE.md](../../docs/CODE_STYLE.md)

## Agent

- Preserve existing style; fix logic only.
- Never add comments in code. Never delete existing comments (author reminders).
- Explanations to user: **Ukrainian**.
- Unity C# unless stated otherwise.

## Naming

- PascalCase public; `_camelCase` private; `SAVE_KEY` for save constants.
- **No abbreviations:** `identifier` not `id`, `amount` not `amt`.
- UI: `UI` prefix (`UICardCollectionPresenter`).
- Suffixes: `System`, `Config`, `Save`, `ItemAsset`, `ItemRuntime`, `ItemSave`.

## Formatting

- Multiline `if` / `else` / `switch` **with braces always**.
- Prefer `foreach`; **no LINQ**.
- `var` only when type is obvious from the right side.

## Examples

```csharp
if (_itemCollection.TryGetValue(identifier, out var runtime))
{
    runtime.Amount.AddValue(amount);
    OnSaveRequired?.Invoke();
}

foreach (var cardItemRuntime in _cardCollection.Values)
{
    result.Add(cardItemRuntime);
}

void ISavable.Load()
{
    var save = SaveLoadStorage.Load<CardSave>(SAVE_KEY);
}

[Inject]
public void Inject(CardSystem cardSystem)
{
    _cardSystem = cardSystem;
}
```

## out parameters

- `out` is fine when the caller uses the value (`TryGetValue`, `TryGetReward`).
- `out _` means this caller does not need that value. Add a `bool` method (`HasClaimableReward`, `IsClaimableReward`).
- Do not discard `out`, and do not implement that method as `return TryGetSomething(out _)`.
- Keep a shared search private. Each public method returns only what its caller uses.

## Interfaces

- Explicit: `void ISavable.Load()`, `void IInitializable.Initialize()`.
- MonoBehaviour: `[Inject]` method, not constructor.

## Systems

- After persisted mutation: `OnSaveRequired?.Invoke()`.
- See [docs/SYSTEMS.md](../../docs/SYSTEMS.md) for Load / Initialize.
